   {:id "original-base-k-297-sheep-farmer" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "K" :number "297" :type "Occupation" :name "Sheep Farmer" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you take Sheep with one of your people, you receive an additional Sheep from the supply. You can exchange 3 Sheep for 1 Cattle and 1 Wild boar at any time (except during the breeding phase.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-base-k-298-shepherd-boy" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "K" :number "298" :type "Occupation" :name "Shepherd Boy" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Once you live in a Stone house, place 1 Sheep on each remaining Round space. At the start of these rounds, you receive the Sheep. (If you already live in a Stone house, place the Sheep immediately.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-base-k-299-slaughterman" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "K" :number "299" :type "Occupation" :name "Slaughterman" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever another player converts animals to Food, you receive 1 Food from the supply. In the Feeding phase, you are the last player to feed your family (so you can benefit if other players slaughter.)(If you slaughter, you receive no additional Food.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-base-k-300-schnaps-distiller" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "K" :number "300" :type "Occupation" :name "Schnaps Distiller" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "In the Feeding phase of each Harvest, you can convert up to 1 Vegetable to 5 Food." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-base-k-301-wood-carver" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "K" :number "301" :type "Occupation" :name "Wood Carver" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "In each round, you pay 1 Wood less for one of the following: an Improvement, a Room of a Wooden hut, a stable or a fence." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-base-k-302-pig-whisperer" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "K" :number "302" :type "Occupation" :name "Pig Whisperer" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Add 4,7 and 10 to the current round and place 1 Wild boar on each corresponding Round space. At the start of these rounds, you receive the Wild boar." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-base-k-303-stone-breaker" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "K" :number "303" :type "Occupation" :name "Stone Breaker" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "At any time, you can Renovate your Clay hut to a Stone house without using the \"Renovation\" Action space. (You must still pay the costs of the renovation.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-base-k-304-veterinarian" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "K" :number "304" :type "Occupation" :name "Veterinarian" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "When you play this card, place 4 Sheep, 3 Wild boar and 2 Cattle in a container. At the start of each round, draw two animals. If they are the same, keep one. Return the 1 or 2 animals to the container." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-base-k-305-animal-handler" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "K" :number "305" :type "Occupation" :name "Animal Handler" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Place 1 Sheep on the space for Round 7, 1 Wild boar on Round 10, and 1 Cattle on Round 14. At the start of these rounds, you can buy the animal for 1 Food." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-base-k-306-animal-tamer" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "K" :number "306" :type "Occupation" :name "Animal Tamer" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "You can keep 1 animal in each room of your home. You may keep more than 1 type of animal in your home." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-base-k-307-animal-breeder" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "K" :number "307" :type "Occupation" :name "Animal Breeder" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you fence unused spaces to create at least one new pasture, you can buy a pair of animals: 2 Sheep for 1 Food, 2 Wild boar for 2 Food, or 2 Cattle for 3 Food." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-base-k-308-foreman" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "K" :number "308" :type "Occupation" :name "Foreman" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "At the start of the Work phase, you can place 1 Food from the general supply on an Action space of your choice." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-base-k-309-weaver" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "K" :number "309" :type "Occupation" :name "Weaver" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you have at least 2 Sheep at the start of the Work phase, you receive 1 Food." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-base-k-310-resource-seller" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "K" :number "310" :type "Occupation" :name "Resource Seller" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Pile (from bottom to top) 1 Stone, Clay, Stone, Clay, Reed, Clay, Wood on this card. You receive the top marker when you receive that type of building resource." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-base-k-311-magician" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "K" :number "311" :type "Occupation" :name "Magician" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use your last person to choose the \"Traveling Players\" action on an Action space, you receive an additional 1 Grain and 1 Food." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-base-k-312-fence-overseer" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "K" :number "312" :type "Occupation" :name "Fence Overseer" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Each round, for a cost of 1 Food, you can immediately Fence a pasture of 1 farmyard space around a stable that you just built. You do not need to pay Wood for the fences." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-base-k-339-pelts" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "K" :number "339" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Pelts" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "3 Occupations" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "For each Animal that you slaughter and return to the general supply, you may place 1 Food from your personal supply in 1 of your rooms. You may have a maximum of 1 Food in each room. You cannot use these Food any more, but each is worth 1 Bonus point at the end of the game." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-base-k-342-animal-trainer" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "K" :number "342" :type "Occupation" :name "Animal Trainer" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you take food from a \"Traveling Players\" space, you may immediately use it to buy animals: Pay 2 Food for each Sheep or Wild Boar and 3 Food for each Cattle." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-base-z-313-stump-jump-plow" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "Z" :number "313" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Stump-Jump Plow" :min-players 1 :cost-text "2 Wood" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Once you live in a Clay hut or Stone house, whenever you use a Family member's action to take Wood you can pay 1 Food to Plow 1 field." :printed-cost {:wood 2}}
   {:id "original-base-z-314-keg" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "Z" :number "314" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Keg" :min-players 1 :cost-text "1 Wood" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? true :text "Once all the Family members have been placed in this round, you may place a Guest marker to carry out an additional Action." :printed-cost {:wood 1}}
   {:id "original-base-z-315-brewer-s-copper" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "Z" :number "315" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Brewer's Copper" :min-players 1 :cost-text "1 Grain,1 Stone" :prerequisites "" :points-text "1" :passing? false :text "During the Feeding phase of each Harvest, you can use the Brewer's Copper to convert at most 1 Grain to 2 Food. At the end of the game, you receive 1 Bonus point if you have at least 7 Grain." :printed-cost {:grain 1 :stone 1}}
   {:id "original-base-z-316-bust" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "Z" :number "316" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Bust" :min-players 1 :cost-text "1 Stone" :prerequisites "see below" :points-text "2" :passing? false :text "The Bust cannot be carved (this card cannot be played) once all other players have 2 or more Occupations. (3 Occupations in a 3-player game, 4 Occupations in a 2-player game)." :printed-cost {:stone 1}}
   {:id "original-base-z-317-family-portrait" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "Z" :number "317" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Family Portrait" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? true :text "Pay 2 Food for each of your Family members, and receive 4 Bonus points. (Write them on the scoring pad)." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-base-z-318-barbecue" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "Z" :number "318" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Barbecue" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? true :text "When you play this card, you can convert as many Animals to Food as you have Family members. For each Sheep, you receive 3 Food, for each Wild boar, 4 and for each Cattle, 5." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-base-z-319-pumpkin-seed-oil" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "Z" :number "319" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Pumpkin Seed Oil" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "Have 1 Vegetable Field" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Three times during the game (at most once per round), you can place 1 Vegetable on this card and receive 3 Food in exchange. The Vegetable(s) on this card are counted in the scoring at the end of the game." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-base-z-320-maypole" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "Z" :number "320" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Maypole" :min-players 1 :cost-text "1 Wood" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Play this card before the end of Round 4. When you play this card, place one of your unbuilt fences upright on an unused farmyard space. If you have not knocked it over by the end of the game, you earn 2 Bonus points. (The farmyard space counts as \"used\".) (If another player knocks it over, you can replace it)" :printed-cost {:wood 1}}
   {:id "original-base-z-321-ranch" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "Z" :number "321" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Ranch" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "All farmyard spaces are used" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "For each Round that has not yet begun when you play this card, you receive 1 Bonus point and 2 Food. (Write the Bonus point(s) on the scoring pad.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-base-z-322-dozing-bull" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "Z" :number "322" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Dozing Bull" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "As long as you have at least 1 Cattle in your farm, you can knock down your fences and rebuild them at any time, for no cost. (Your animals do not run away.) (Fences must always be placed according to the rules.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-base-z-323-giant-pumpkin" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "Z" :number "323" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Giant Pumpkin" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Place 1 Vegetable from your own supply on this card. At any time, you can Harvest this Vegetable and convert it to Food. If it is still on the card at the end of the game, you receive 2 Bonus points. (You can count the Vegetable in scoring at the end of the game.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-base-z-324-scarecrow" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "Z" :number "324" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Scarecrow" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "2 empty fields" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you Sow, you can pay 1 Wood and Sow 2 Grain instead of 1 on an empty field." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-base-z-325-village-beauty" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "Z" :number "325" :type "Occupation" :name "Village Beauty" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "At any time, you can play 3 Food to take a \"Family growth\" action without placing one of your Family members. You must have room in your home. You can use the Newborn to take action from the following round." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-base-z-326-gentleman" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "Z" :number "326" :type "Occupation" :name "Gentleman" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you manage to be the very last player to place a Family member in any round, you receive 1 Food after you take the final action. If you play the Gentleman card with the last Family member to be placed during the current round, you receive 2 Food." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-base-z-327-herald" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "Z" :number "327" :type "Occupation" :name "Herald" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "At any time, you may look at all the remaining unplaced Round cards and re-sort them. (Cards must remain in the appropriate game stage.) When you play this card, you receive 2 Wood." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-base-z-328-cooper" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "Z" :number "328" :type "Occupation" :name "Cooper" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you or another player receives more than 2 Food from an Action space, you receive 1 Food from the General supply." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-base-z-329-mail-coach-driver" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "Z" :number "329" :type "Occupation" :name "Mail Coach Driver" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "From now until the end of the game, the other players only receive goods from Action spaces when they return their Family members to their home. (This card applies to goods that are on Action spaces as well as goods that are taken from the Supply, but not to goods that are received from cards.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-base-z-330-taxidermist" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "Z" :number "330" :type "Occupation" :name "Taxidermist" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "When you convert Animals to Food, you can place (some of) them on this card instead of returning them to the Supply. The card can hold a maximum of 1 Sheep, 1 Wild boar and 1 Cattle. These animals are counted in scoring." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-base-z-331-sower" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "Z" :number "331" :type "Occupation" :name "Sower" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "You may immediately Sow each Vegetable that you receive outside the Harvest phase and would otherwise place in your Supply." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-base-z-332-seed-trader" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "Z" :number "332" :type "Occupation" :name "Seed Trader" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Place 2 Grain and 2 Vegetables on this card. You may buy them at any time. Each Grain costs 2 Food, each Vegetable costs 3 Food." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-base-z-333-game-designer" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "Z" :number "333" :type "Occupation" :name "Game Designer" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "You can exchange 1 Wood, 1 Clay, 1 Reed and 1 Stone for 2 Food and 1 Bonus point at any time and as often as you like. (Note the Bonus points in the appropriate section of the scoring pad.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-base-z-334-dance-instructor" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "Z" :number "334" :type "Occupation" :name "Dance Instructor" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "You receive 4 Food before you pay the costs of playing this Occupation. Immediately return this card to your hand." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-base-z-335-cube-cutter" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "Z" :number "335" :type "Occupation" :name "Cube Cutter" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "During the Field phase of each Harvest, you can exchange 1 Wood and 1 Food for 1 Bonus point. (Note the Bonus points in the appropriate section of the scoring pad.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-base-z-336-mother-of-twins" :edition "Original" :pack "Base" :deck "Z" :number "336" :type "Occupation" :name "Mother of Twins" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "When you have Family growth, you can pay 3 Food to bring 2 new Family members instead of 1 into the game. You need only have space for 1 Family member in your home." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-promotion-fl-61-brakelhuhner" :edition "Original" :pack "Promotion" :deck "FL" :number "61" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Brakelhuhner" :min-players 1 :cost-text "2 Food" :prerequisites "" :points-text "*" :passing? false :text "Lege 2 NW aus deinem allgemeinen Vorrat auf diese Karte. Solange in der Erntephase mindestens 2 NW auf der Karte liegen, lege 1 NW aus dem allgemeinen Vorrat dazu. Du kannst jederzeit NW von der Karte in deinen eignen Vorrat legen. *2 Siegpunkte bei mindestens 4 NW auf der Karte" :printed-cost {:food 2}}
   {:id "original-expansion-bi-1-alm" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "BI" :number "1" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Alm" :min-players 1 :cost-text "1 Sheep" :prerequisites "" :points-text "1" :passing? false :text "When you play this card, you may remove 1 stable from your farmyard and receive 1 Cattle. This card can hold an unlimited number of Cattle. (This card does not count as a pasture when scoring)." :printed-cost {:sheep 1}}
   {:id "original-expansion-bi-1-sparrenburg-castle" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "BI" :number "1" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Sparrenburg Castle" :min-players 1 :cost-text "1 Wood,1 Clay,2 Stone" :prerequisites "2 Occupations" :points-text "2" :passing? false :text "Whenever anyone uses a Wood/Stone Accumulation space, place 1 Wood/Stone from the general supply on this card. Whenever you place a person on a \"Renovation\" Action space, take up to 5 resources from this card. (Before scoring, discard all the resources from this card.)" :printed-cost {:wood 1 :clay 1 :stone 2}}
   {:id "original-expansion-bi-2-bielefeld-playing-cards" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "BI" :number "2" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Bielefeld Playing Cards" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "No Occupations" :points-text "5" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use an Accumulation space, place all the items received on this card instead of placing them in your supply. Whenever there is 4 or more of the same item on this card, move exactly 4 of those to your supply. (Before scoring, discard the items on this card.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-bi-3-baking-powder" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "BI" :number "3" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Baking Powder" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "1 Baking Improvement" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use the \"Sow and/or Bake Bread\" Action space, place 1 Grain from the supply on each of your Major Improvements. Whenever you play an Occupation, move these Grain to your supply. (Before scoring, discard the Grain from your Major Improvements.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-bi-4-spielwiese" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "BI" :number "4" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Spielwiese" :min-players 1 :cost-text "1 Food" :prerequisites "At most 1 Occupation" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Reveal 2 Occupations randomly from the deck and add them to your hand. Look at the player size number on each card (either 1, 3, or 4). Take as many different Building resources as the smaller of the two numbers." :printed-cost {:food 1}}
   {:id "original-expansion-bi-5-home-zoo" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "BI" :number "5" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Home Zoo" :min-players 1 :cost-text "1 Wood,1 Clay" :prerequisites "" :points-text "1" :passing? false :text "This card can hold up to 1 Sheep, 1 Wild boar and 1 Cattle. You may only place animals here when you receive them from Accumulation spaces. While here, they do not participate in the Breeding phase of Harvest. During the last Harvest, you may exchange animals here for 1 Bonus point each." :printed-cost {:wood 1 :clay 1}}
   {:id "original-expansion-bi-6-conspiracy" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "BI" :number "6" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Conspiracy" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "1 BI-Deck card" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "In the Field phase of each Harvest, you receive 1 Food for every 2 BI-Deck cards you have played. At the end of the game, every player receives 1/2/3 Bonus points for 1/3/5 played BI-Deck cards." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-bi-7-ravensberger-spinning-mill" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "BI" :number "7" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Ravensberger Spinning Mill" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "1 Sheep" :points-text "1" :passing? false :text "When you play this card, each other player may take 2 Food from the supply. For each player that takes 2 Food, you may pay 1 Building resource to the supply for 1 Bonus point. All paid resources must be different." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-bi-8-custard" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "BI" :number "8" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Custard" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "1 Cooking Improvement" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "You immediately receive 1 Food for every Harvest remaining when you play this card. Whenever you take Stone from an Accumulation space leave 1 Stone on the space." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-bi-10-the-52nd-latitude" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "BI" :number "10" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "The 52nd Latitude" :min-players 1 :cost-text "1 Wood,1 Stone" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Immediately place 1 Stone from the general supply on 1 unused farmyard space. (It now counts as used.) At the end of the game, you receive 1 Bonus point for each empty plowed field orthogonally adjacent to this Stone." :printed-cost {:wood 1 :stone 1}}
   {:id "original-expansion-bi-11-schlachter-church" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "BI" :number "11" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Schlachter Church" :min-players 1 :cost-text "1 Wood,1 Clay,1 Stone" :prerequisites "2 animal types" :points-text "1" :passing? false :text "Whenever another player converts an animal to Food with a Cooking Improvement, place it on this card. At any time, you may convert all the animals on this card to 1 Food each. Afterward, this card loses its function but still counts as an Improvement." :printed-cost {:wood 1 :clay 1 :stone 1}}
   {:id "original-expansion-bi-12-skybridge" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "BI" :number "12" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Skybridge" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "Stone house" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Immediately place Stone from your supply between any adjacent rooms of your home. Between each 2 rooms you may place exactly 1 Stone. In the Feeding phase of each Harvest, you receive 1 Grain for each placed Stone. At the end of the game, you receive 1 Bonus point for each placed Stone." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-bi-13-wooden-buttons" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "BI" :number "13" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Wooden Buttons" :min-players 1 :cost-text "1 Wood" :prerequisites "2 empty rooms" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Immediately take 1 Guest token for each empty room in your home. Place these Guests as you would additional Family members and return them at the end of this round. You do not have room for offspring this round." :printed-cost {:wood 1}}
   {:id "original-expansion-bi-14-linen-weaver" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "BI" :number "14" :type "Occupation" :name "Linen Weaver" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "At the start of each round, this Occupation is passed left to the next player. It only counts as a played Occupation for the player who has it. All their Improvement costs are reduced by 1 Wood. When the original player has it, their Improvement costs are reduced by 1 Clay, 1 Stone, and 1 Reed also." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-bi-15-vampire" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "BI" :number "15" :type "Occupation" :name "Vampire" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Play this card only if the player on your right just used an Accumulation space on the previous turn. You immediately use the same Action and receive the same amount of items. Take the items from the general supply." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-bi-16-institute-founder" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "BI" :number "16" :type "Occupation" :name "Institute Founder" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "When you play this card, you may immediately pay 1 Food for 1 Grain. In the Feeding phase of each Harvest, your 4th and 5th Family members need only 1 Food." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-bi-17-white-brazilian" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "BI" :number "17" :type "Occupation" :name "White Brazilian" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Play this card only if your top 5 farmyard spaces are unused. Place 1 stable and 1 Wild boar on the leftmost or rightmost farmyard space in this row. Flip a coin. If the coin lands heads, keep both the Wild boar and stable, otherwise keep only the stable." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-bi-18-apple-man" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "BI" :number "18" :type "Occupation" :name "Apple Man" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Once during each Returning home phase, you may pay 1 Vegetable from your supply to take a \"Plow 1 field\", \"Build fences\", or \"Build stables\" action without placing a person." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-bi-19-deaconess" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "BI" :number "19" :type "Occupation" :name "Deaconess" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "As long as you have exactly 2 Family members, in the Feeding phase of Harvest 1/2/3/4/5/6, you receive 1/2/3/4/5/6 Food." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-bi-20-survivalist" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "BI" :number "20" :type "Occupation" :name "Survivalist" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "(Your Family will eat anything.) In the Feeding phase of each Harvest, the Survivalist can convert up to 1 of each Building material (Wood, Clay, Reed, and Stone) to 2 Food each. In each Harvest you use this, place 1 of these Food on the \"Fishing\" Action space." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-bi-21-advisor" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "BI" :number "21" :type "Occupation" :name "Advisor" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "The next time you use the \"Fishing\" Action space with a person, you also receive 2 Bonus points. After that, you receive 1 Bonus point whenever you use the \"Fishing\" Action space with a person." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-bi-22-protest-singer" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "BI" :number "22" :type "Occupation" :name "Protest Singer" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "(Your system has no limits.) You may keep 1 animal on each unused space on your farmyard. (The spaces still count as unused.) These animals do not participate in the Breeding phase of Harvest." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-bi-23-systems-theorist" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "BI" :number "23" :type "Occupation" :name "Systems Theorist" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you build at least 1 stable, you receive 1 Food. At the end of the game, you receive 1/2/3 Bonus points for 2/3/4 stables adjacent to each other." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-bi-24-member-of-a-co-operative" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "BI" :number "24" :type "Occupation" :name "Member of a Co-operative" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever another player performs a \"Family growth\" action, you may place 1 Food from the supply on this card. Once during a 3/4/5 player game, you may pay 3/4/5 Food from this card to play your next \"Family growth\" action as \"Family growth even without room\"." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-c1d393d1-1-governor" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Č" :number "1" :type "Occupation" :name "Governor" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Immediately take the 4 top Occupations from the face-down pile and select two of them. You may (if you fulfil the conditions on the card) immediately play one at no cost; placed the other into your hand. If you cannot or choose not to play either, take both into your hand." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-c1d393d1-2-weekend-worker" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Č" :number "2" :type "Occupation" :name "Weekend Worker" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you renovate, you can build 1 additional room by paying 1 Reed, 1 of the basic Building resource for the hut (Wood or Clay) and 2 Building resources of the new home type (Clay or Stone)." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-c1d393d1-3-jack-of-all-trades" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Č" :number "3" :type "Occupation" :name "Jack-of-all-Trades" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Immediately discard all the Occupations that you have played. (All their effects are lost.) Once in each Round, you can pay 1 Food to use an Occupation that has been played by another player. You receive all benefits except for any that are given when the card is played or at the end of the game. As soon as you play another Occupation, you must discard the Jack-of-all-Trades." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-c1d393d1-4-teacher-of-nations" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Č" :number "4" :type "Occupation" :name "Teacher of Nations" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "All players can pay 1 Food less when they play an Occupation. Whenever one of the other players use this discount, you receive 1 Food from the Supply." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-c1d393d1-5-hero" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Č" :number "5" :type "Occupation" :name "Hero" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "You immediately receive 3 Food. Once during the game, you can discard 1 Wild Boar to immediately take a \"Family Growth\" action without placing a Family member. The newborn Family member cannot take an Action until the following round, and requires a room in your Home." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-c1d393d1-6-seeress" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Č" :number "6" :type "Occupation" :name "Seeress" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "You immediately receive 1 Stone from the Supply and look at the top 3 cards in the Round card pile, then return them in your choice of order. (You need not match these cards to the Phase of the game.) In addition, at any time during the game, you can look at the top Round card." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-c1d393d1-7-bureaucrat" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Č" :number "7" :type "Occupation" :name "Bureaucrat" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Place up to 3 Food from your own Supply onto this card. Once during each Round, you may pay 1 Food from this card to place a Person on an Action space that already holds 1 Person (whether your own or another player's). (You can take the Food from this card back into your Supply at any time.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-c1d393d1-8-bagpiper" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Č" :number "8" :type "Occupation" :name "Bagpiper" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "You immediately receive 2 Food. The Family member that took the \"Occupation\" action returns home as though it had not done any work yet this Round. (You place this Family member again as soon as it is your turn again.) The \"Occupation\" Action space returns to its unoccupied state and may be used again." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-c1d393d1-9-only-child" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Č" :number "9" :type "Occupation" :name "Only Child" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "If there are still 3/6/9 full Rounds to be played, you immediately receive 1/2/3 Wood. You receive 3 Bonus points if you have exactly 3 Family members on your farmyard at the end of the game. (Guest markers are not counted as Family members.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-c1d393d1-10-snitch" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Č" :number "10" :type "Occupation" :name "Snitch" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Immediately flip 1 Occupation that you have played face down. In exchange, you can choose to take either 5 Food or 1 Cattle from the Supply. You lose all effects of the face down occupation. (For future Occupations and Improvements, this Occupation continues to count as \"played\".)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-c1d393d1-11-robber" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Č" :number "11" :type "Occupation" :name "Robber" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Once during each Round, when it is your turn, you may skip placing a Family Member. Instead, choose to take 1 Food or 1 Wood from the Supply. You can only skip your turn if at least 1 other player has 1 or more Person tokens to place." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-c1d393d1-12-saint-nicholas" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Č" :number "12" :type "Occupation" :name "Saint Nicholas" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Count how many Family members have been born during the game so far, and immediately take that many Food (maximum 6). (New Offspring, who are still on the \"Family growth\" space already count as Family members.) All players with the fewest Offspring (which could include you) immediately receive 1 Vegetable each." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-c1d393d1-13-golden-hands" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Č" :number "13" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Golden Hands" :min-players 1 :cost-text "1 Food" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you play a Minor or Major improvement, you may replace exactly 1 building resource with another." :printed-cost {:food 1}}
   {:id "original-expansion-c1d393d1-14-schoolhouse" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Č" :number "14" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Schoolhouse" :min-players 1 :cost-text "1 Wood,1 Clay" :prerequisites "" :points-text "1" :passing? false :text "At any time, instead of playing 1 Minor or Major Improvement, you may play 1 Occupation. The price of this Occupation is 1 Food." :printed-cost {:wood 1 :clay 1}}
   {:id "original-expansion-c1d393d1-15-beer-festival" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Č" :number "15" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Beer Festival" :min-players 1 :cost-text "1 Food" :prerequisites "Have 3 or more Family members" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "When you play this card, you can immediately take the \"Bake Bread\" action. If you have at least 3/6/9 Food left at the end of the game, you receive 1/2/3 Bonus points." :printed-cost {:food 1}}
   {:id "original-expansion-c1d393d1-16-wagon-fort" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Č" :number "16" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Wagon Fort" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "For each empty space on your Farmyard, you can pay 1 Wood and place 1 of your unbuilt Fences on it. You can take any of these Fences back into your supply at any time. If the Fences are still there at the end of the game, the spaces count as used." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-c1d393d1-17-chapel" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Č" :number "17" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Chapel" :min-players 1 :cost-text "2 Clay" :prerequisites "" :points-text "1" :passing? false :text "The Chapel is an additional Action space. Players who use this Action can return up to 2 Begging cards. Each Begging card costs 1 Stone, which is placed on the Chapel. At the end of the game, each Stone on this card is worth 1 Bonus point." :printed-cost {:clay 2}}
   {:id "original-expansion-c1d393d1-18-hops-field" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Č" :number "18" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Hops Field" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "Have 1 empty Field" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "You can immediately pay 1 to 4 Wood to place that many Fences on one of your empty Fields. This Field can no longer be Sown, but is counted as a Field at the end of the game. For each Fence on the Field, you immediately receive 1 Food and you receive 1 Bonus point at the end of the game." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-c1d393d1-19-wine-cellar" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Č" :number "19" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Wine Cellar" :min-players 1 :cost-text "2 Stone" :prerequisites "Have 1 unfenced Stable" :points-text "1" :passing? false :text "Immediately convert 1 unfenced Stable into a Wine Cellar by tipping it onto its side. You cannot hold animals in the Stable anymore. In the Field phase of each Harvest, you receive 2 Food from the Supply. The space is counted as used. The Wine Cellar is not counted as a Stable. If you fence the space, you can use it as a Pasture." :printed-cost {:stone 2}}
   {:id "original-expansion-c1d393d1-20-golem" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Č" :number "20" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Golem" :min-players 1 :cost-text "2 Clay" :prerequisites "Have 1 Oven or Cooking Hearth" :points-text "1" :passing? false :text "Place the 2 Clay you paid for this card on it. At the start of each of the next 2 Rounds, return 1 Clay from this card to the Supply. In these 2 Rounds, the first Family member that you place uses that space twice in a row. On Accumulating spaces, this means that for the second action you can take as many of the resource as are replenished each Round from the Supply." :printed-cost {:clay 2}}
   {:id "original-expansion-c1d393d1-21-venus-of-dolni-vestonice" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Č" :number "21" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Venus of Dolni Vestonice" :min-players 1 :cost-text "2 Clay" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use the action space \"Family Growth and Minor Improvement\", you may carry out the family growth action twice with that person. (The Action space becomes available in Rounds 5-7. Even if you take the Action twice, you can build at most 1 Minor Improvement.)" :printed-cost {:clay 2}}
   {:id "original-expansion-c1d393d1-22-bible" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Č" :number "22" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Bible" :min-players 1 :cost-text "1 Wood" :prerequisites "Have 1 Occupation" :points-text "1" :passing? false :text "Each of your Family members who takes one of the following Actions in a Round that ends with a Harvest requires 1 Food fewer during the Harvest: \"Plow fields\", \"Plow fields and Sow\", \"Take 1 Grain\", \"Take 1 Vegetable\" or \"Day Labor\"." :printed-cost {:wood 1}}
   {:id "original-expansion-c1d393d1-23-hunger-wall" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Č" :number "23" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Hunger Wall" :min-players 1 :cost-text "3 Clay" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "During each Harvest, each Player can pay 1 Clay instead of the required 2 Food for exactly 1 Family member. All that Clay paid is placed on this card. At the end of the game, you receive 1 Bonus point for every 2 Clay on the card." :printed-cost {:clay 3}}
   {:id "original-expansion-c1d393d1-24-five-year-plan" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Č" :number "24" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Five-Year-Plan" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "Have 2 Occupations and 1 empty Field" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Mark 1 empty Field with a green arrow marker. You will never be able to Sow this field. The marked Field is no longer scored as a Field but only as a used Farmyard space. You can immediately Sow your remaining empty Fields. Place 2 additional Grain or Vegetables on each Field that you plant this way." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-fl-1-farm-cart" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "FL" :number "1" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Farm Cart" :min-players 1 :cost-text "3 Wood" :prerequisites "" :points-text "1" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use the \"Sow\" action, you can Sow 1 Grain on an existing Vegetable field or 1 Vegetable on an existing Grain field. (You can have at most 1 pile of Vegetables and 1 pile Grain on each field.)" :printed-cost {:wood 3}}
   {:id "original-expansion-fl-2-beguine-courtyard" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "FL" :number "2" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Beguine Courtyard" :min-players 1 :cost-text "2 Stone,2 Clay" :prerequisites "" :points-text "1" :passing? false :text "Once your home is shaped like the picture below (5 room home shaped like a \"C\"), you must immediately move all the people still in your supply into your home. They may take actions starting that round. (They count as adult Family members and not \"newborns\".)" :printed-cost {:stone 2 :clay 2}}
   {:id "original-expansion-fl-3-belgian-shepherd" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "FL" :number "3" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Belgian Shepherd" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "1 Sheep" :points-text "1" :passing? false :text "You may keep up to 2 Sheep on exactly 1 Unused space in your farmyard. The space still counts as unused. You may not keep any animal other than the Belgian Shepherd in your home. (Even if you have special Occupations or Improvements.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-fl-4-educational-building" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "FL" :number "4" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Educational Building" :min-players 1 :cost-text "2 Clay,1 Reed" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "This card is an additional Action space for you only. The first time you use your 3rd and/or 4th Family member this game, you may use it on this card and alternate placing 1 Wood and 1 Stone on each remaining Round space. Start with Wood. At the start of these rounds, you receive the resource." :printed-cost {:clay 2 :reed 1}}
   {:id "original-expansion-fl-5-brabant" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "FL" :number "5" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Brabant" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "At the end of the game, you receive 5 Bonus points if have 2 or 3 animal categories where you score 1 negative point. (You still lose the points for the missing animal types.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-fl-6-endive-field" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "FL" :number "6" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Endive Field" :min-players 1 :cost-text "2 Food" :prerequisites "2 Occupations" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "When you play this card, you receive 1 Vegetable. In Rounds that end with a Harvest, you may Sow Vegetables on this card as if it were 1 field. (This card counts as a field but not for scoring.)" :printed-cost {:food 2}}
   {:id "original-expansion-fl-7-diamond-trading-post" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "FL" :number "7" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Diamond Trading Post" :min-players 1 :cost-text "3 Wood,3 Clay" :prerequisites "3 Occupations" :points-text "1" :passing? false :text "Place 3 Stone from the general supply on this card. At any time, you can move these Stone in your supply. At the start of each Harvest, if you have more Stone in your supply than there are on this card, you may return 1 Stone on this card for a pair of animals. You receive Sheep/ Wild boar/ Cattle with the 1st/ 2nd/ 3rd return." :printed-cost {:wood 3 :clay 3}}
   {:id "original-expansion-fl-8-wooden-draisine" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "FL" :number "8" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Wooden Draisine" :min-players 1 :cost-text "2 Wood" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "You can use 2 orthogonally adjacent Accumulation spaces on the same game board with 1 person by placing the person between the spaces. (Afterward, both spaces count as occupied.) You must leave 2 of the items on each space." :printed-cost {:wood 2}}
   {:id "original-expansion-fl-9-ebony-shoe" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "FL" :number "9" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Ebony Shoe" :min-players 1 :cost-text "1 Wood" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "If there are still 1/3/6/9 rounds to play, you immediately receive 1/2/3/4 Clay. After playing this card, the next player to have no Unused farmyard spaces receives 3 Bonus points." :printed-cost {:wood 1}}
   {:id "original-expansion-fl-10-stuck-cart" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "FL" :number "10" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Stuck Cart" :min-players 1 :cost-text "2 Food" :prerequisites "2 people placed" :points-text "" :passing? true :text "Immediately place and use all the Family members that are in your home. (Afterward, play continues as normal. This card can only be played during the Work phase.)" :printed-cost {:food 2}}
   {:id "original-expansion-fl-11-towhead" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "FL" :number "11" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Towhead" :min-players 1 :cost-text "1 Food" :prerequisites "Round 4 or before" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Place the \"After Family growth also 1 Minor Improvement\" Action space face-down on Round 6. In Round 5, you can use it as if it were already face-up (in addition to the regular new Action space in Round 5)." :printed-cost {:food 1}}
   {:id "original-expansion-fl-12-cart" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "FL" :number "12" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Cart" :min-players 1 :cost-text "3 Wood" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever there are at least 6 Wood, 5 Clay, 4 Reed, or 3 Stone on an Action space, only you can take this space with your first person in the Work phase." :printed-cost {:wood 3}}
   {:id "original-expansion-fl-13-gift-table" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "FL" :number "13" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Gift Table" :min-players 1 :cost-text "1 Wood" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Pile 1 of each on this card (from bottom to top) : Vegetable, Wood, Sheep, Wood, Grain. At any time, you may buy the top item for 1 Food. When you buy the Sheep: it moves to your supply, it can be exchanged for 2 Food at any time, it does not breed, and it counts for scoring." :printed-cost {:wood 1}}
   {:id "original-expansion-fl-14-jenever-distillery" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "FL" :number "14" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Jenever Distillery" :min-players 1 :cost-text "3 Clay,1 Stone" :prerequisites "" :points-text "1" :passing? false :text "When you play this card, place 1 to 4 Wood from your supply on this card. You can move this Wood back to your supply at any time. In the Field phase of each Harvest, you receive 1 Food for each Wood on this card (without removing the Wood)." :printed-cost {:clay 3 :stone 1}}
   {:id "original-expansion-fl-15-courtyard-garden" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "FL" :number "15" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Courtyard Garden" :min-players 1 :cost-text "3 Wood,1 Stone" :prerequisites "Wooden Hut" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "At the end of the game, you receive 2 Bonus points for each Unused farmyard space orthogonally adjacent to your Stone house. (These spaces still count as unused when scoring.)" :printed-cost {:wood 3 :stone 1}}
   {:id "original-expansion-fl-16-jeanneke-pis" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "FL" :number "16" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Jeanneke-Pis" :min-players 1 :cost-text "1 Stone" :prerequisites "Have a Well" :points-text "1" :passing? false :text "Your Well is an additional Action space for you only. Whenever you use your Well, you activate its effect again. (Wells are cards whose name ends with \"Well\".)" :printed-cost {:stone 1}}
   {:id "original-expansion-fl-17-bobbin-table" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "FL" :number "17" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Bobbin Table" :min-players 1 :cost-text "1 Wood" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "This card is an additional Action space for you only. Whenever you use this space, you may afterward (and until the next Harvest) use Action spaces even if they are occupied." :printed-cost {:wood 1}}
   {:id "original-expansion-fl-18-office" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "FL" :number "18" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Office" :min-players 1 :cost-text "4 Clay,3 Wood,2 Reed" :prerequisites "" :points-text "1" :passing? false :text "At any time, you may exchange 1 Clay for 1 Stone. At any time you may exchange 1 Grain in your supply for 1 Vegetable. At any time you may exchange 1 Wild boar for 1 Cattle." :printed-cost {:clay 4 :wood 3 :reed 2}}
