   {:id "original-expansion-g-12-carrot-farmer" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "12" :type "Occupation" :name "Carrot Farmer" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Place 3 Vegetables from the supply on this card. Whenever you use the \"Plow 1 Field\" Action space, you may pay 1 Food for one of the Vegetables." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-13-clay-starter" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "13" :type "Occupation" :name "Clay Starter" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "When you play this card, if you have only 2 rooms in your Wooden hut, immediately pay 1 Food to renovate it to Clay for free." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-14-early-riser" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "14" :type "Occupation" :name "Early Riser" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "When you play this card, you receive 1 Sheep. For you, the Breeding phase of the Harvest precedes the Field and Feeding phases. You may immediately cook baby animals if you do not have room to keep them." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-15-family-counselor" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "15" :type "Occupation" :name "Family Counselor" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever at the end of a Work phase all of your adult Family members were placed on the same piece of cardboard, you receive 1 Food, if it were 2 Adults. For 3 Adults, you receive 1 Grain. For 4+ Adults, you receive 1 Vegetable." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-16-fence-helper" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "16" :type "Occupation" :name "Fence Helper" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever another player builds at least 1 fence, you may pay that player 1 Food to immediately take the \"Fences\" action. (Pay costs normally)." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-17-fish-seller" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "17" :type "Occupation" :name "Fish Seller" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use the \"Fishing\" Action space, you may use Food that you take from the Action space (but not Fishing cards) to buy up to 2 (same or different) items. One building resource costs 1 Food. One Grain, Sheep or Wild boar costs 2 Food. One Vegetable or Cattle costs 3 Food." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-18-fisherman-s-apprentice" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "18" :type "Occupation" :name "Fisherman's Apprentice" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever another player uses the \"Fishing\" Action space, you may pay that player 1 Food to play an Occupation." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-19-food-critic" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "19" :type "Occupation" :name "Food Critic" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "The next time you use the \"Fishing\" Action space, place 1 Food from the supply on this card. Whenever you Bake bread or convert animals, Vegetables, or building resources to Food, you may place that good on this card. At the end of the game, you receive 1/2/4/6 Bonus points for 4/5/6/7+ different items on this card." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-20-freeloader" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "20" :type "Occupation" :name "Freeloader" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Each round, your first Family member may use an occupied Action space. Your first Family member can never take the \"Starting Player\" Action space. (Even if it is unoccupied)." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-21-hermit" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "21" :type "Occupation" :name "Hermit" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "At the end of the game, you receive 6 Bonus points if this is the only Occupation you have played." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-22-glass-blower" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "22" :type "Occupation" :name "Glass Blower" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "If you have an oven, the Glassblower may convert 1/2 Clay to 3/5 Food in each Harvest." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-23-glutton" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "23" :type "Occupation" :name "Glutton" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "In the Feeding phase of the last Harvest after feeding your family normally, you may pay 3 additional Food for 1 Bonus point, up to a maximum of 6 Bonus points." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-24-grafter" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "24" :type "Occupation" :name "Grafter" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "During the Breeding phase of Harvest, if you have 2 or more Grain in your supply you receive 1 Grain from the supply. If you have 2 or more Vegetables, you receive 1 Vegetable from the supply. (Vegetables and Grains that are planted are not counted.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-25-businesswoman" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "25" :type "Occupation" :name "Businesswoman" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "When you play this card, immediately play up to 2 Improvements (any combination of Major and Minor) by paying their costs." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-26-grain-farmer" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "26" :type "Occupation" :name "Grain Farmer" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you have at least 1/4/7/10 planted Grain at the beginning of the Field phase of a Harvest, you receive 1/2/3/4 Food." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-27-grain-lover" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "27" :type "Occupation" :name "Grain Lover" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "If there are still 7 rounds to play, you may Plow 1 field, which you may immediately Sow with 1 Grain from your supply. At the end of the game, all players with the most Grain receive 2 Bonus points each." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-28-grump" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "28" :type "Occupation" :name "Grump" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "If there are still 1/3/6/9 rounds to play, you immediately receive 1/2/3/4 Wood. At the end of the game, all players with the fewest Family members receive 2 Bonus points each." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-29-harbor-master" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "29" :type "Occupation" :name "Harbor Master" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use the \"Fishing\" Action space, you receive 1 additional Reed. Whenever another player uses the \"Fishing\" Action space, you receive 1 Reed and 1 Food from the supply." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-30-headmaster" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "30" :type "Occupation" :name "Headmaster" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever another player plays an Occupation, place 1 Food from the supply on this card. Whenever you play an Occupation, you may pay any costs using Food from this card. At the end of a 4/5 player game, you receive 1 Bonus point for every 3/4 Food on this card." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-31-helper" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "31" :type "Occupation" :name "Helper" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "You can use any \"Renovate\", \"Build room(s)\", or \"Major Improvement\" Action space, even if another player has already placed a person on it." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-32-hobbyist" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "32" :type "Occupation" :name "Hobbyist" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever another player plays an Occupation, you may pay 1 Food to the general supply to play 1 Minor Improvement, or 2 Food to build 1 Major Improvement. (Pay costs for the Improvement normally.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-33-hoe-maker" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "33" :type "Occupation" :name "Hoe Maker" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you build at least 1 fence, you may also pay 1 Food to Plow 1 field." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-34-inventor" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "34" :type "Occupation" :name "Inventor" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "All Improvements with a printed cost of 4 or more resources cost you 1 less resource of your choice." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-35-job-seeker" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "35" :type "Occupation" :name "Job Seeker" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Once in play, this card does not count as an Occupation for any purpose. Whenever, at the start of a round, you have fewer Occupations than any 2 other players, you may pay 1 Food to immediately play an Occupation. (Occupations played this way may not be returned to the player's hand.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-36-late-bloomer" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "36" :type "Occupation" :name "Late Bloomer" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you have fewer Family members than all of the other players and you have room in your home, you may immediately take a \"Family growth\" action. Place the offspring in an empty room. This Family member is not considered a newborn and may take an action the same round." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-37-late-sleeper" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "37" :type "Occupation" :name "Late Sleeper" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "At the start of each round, announce whether or not you will sleep late. If you sleep late, you place all of your people after everyone else has placed all of theirs, but you may also place a Guest token. (If you choose not to sleep late, you place your people normally.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-38-master-baker-s-apprentice" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "38" :type "Occupation" :name "Master Baker's Apprentice" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "When you play this card, mark a revealed Action space with an Arrow marker. This Action space now has the added text \"and/or Bake Bread.\" Whenever another player Bakes bread using this space, you receive 1 Food from the general supply. When you play this card, you may also take the \"Bake bread\" action." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-39-mathematician" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "39" :type "Occupation" :name "Mathematician" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "From Round 6, if there are Wood Action spaces with the same amount of Wood after refilling each round (at the end of phase 2), you can take 1 Wood from one of those spaces. This also applies to Clay Action spaces. In 5 player games, this also applies to Stone Action spaces. You can take only 1 resource per round." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-40-miner" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "40" :type "Occupation" :name "Miner" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use the \"Day Laborer\" Action space, you can take all the Stone markers from one of the \"1 Stone\" Action spaces (stage 2 or stage 4) in the Returning home phase (phase 4)." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-41-mooch" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "41" :type "Occupation" :name "Mooch" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "When you play this card, choose another player. Until the end of the next Harvest, you may convert animals, Vegetables, Grain, and building resources to Food as if you owned the chosen player's Improvements in addition to yours. (The chosen player may use their Improvements normally.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-42-oldest-occupation" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "42" :type "Occupation" :name "Oldest Occupation" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "From Round 5, whenever any player uses the \"Day Laborer\" Action space, they may pay you 2 Food to immediately take a \"Family Growth\" action. (They must have room in their home. If you use Day Laborer, you may grow for free.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-43-opportunist" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "43" :type "Occupation" :name "Opportunist" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use your last action in a round to take one or more types of building resources that have not yet been taken this Work phase, you receive 1 additional resource of one of those types." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-44-pearl-seeker" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "44" :type "Occupation" :name "Pearl Seeker" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use the \"Fishing\" Action space you receive 1 additional Stone. Also, you can use Food that you take from the Action space (but not Fishing cards) to buy more Stone. Each Stone costs 2 Food." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-45-pilgrim" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "45" :type "Occupation" :name "Pilgrim" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "You receive 2 Food before you pay the costs of playing this Occupation. At the start of a round, if you have no building resources, you may take 1 building resource from the supply. At the start of a round, if you have no Food, you may take 1 Food from the supply. (At any time, you may move resources from your personal supply to the general supply.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-46-pond-watchman" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "46" :type "Occupation" :name "Pond Watchman" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "At the end of a round, after all other players have taken their actions, you may pay 1 Food to move one of your people that used the \"Fishing\" Action space this round to a free Wood Action space and take that action." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-47-resource-collector" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "47" :type "Occupation" :name "Resource Collector" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Place 1 Wood, 1 Clay, 1 Reed, and 1 Stone on the next 4 Round spaces in any order you choose. At the start of those rounds, you receive the resource." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-48-ringmaster" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "48" :type "Occupation" :name "Ringmaster" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use the \"Traveling Players\" action on an Action space, you may either play a Minor Improvement or you may pay 1 Grain to build a Major Improvement immediately afterward. (Pay costs for the Improvement normally.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-49-seed-master" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "49" :type "Occupation" :name "Seed Master" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "At any time, you may pay 1 Food to convert 1 Grain in your supply to 1 Vegetable. At any time, you may convert 1 Vegetable in your supply to 1 Grain." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-50-singer" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "50" :type "Occupation" :name "Singer" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "When you play this card, you receive 2 (same or different) building resources of your choice." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-51-stone-deliveryman" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "51" :type "Occupation" :name "Stone Deliveryman" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Place 1 Stone on each of the spaces for Rounds 8, 10, 12, and 14. At the start of these rounds, you receive the Stone." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-52-stone-trader" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "52" :type "Occupation" :name "Stone Trader" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use an action to take Stone, you may immediately afterward pay 1 Food to play an Improvement that has a printed Stone cost. (Pay costs for the Improvement normally.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-53-stonepiler" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "53" :type "Occupation" :name "Stonepiler" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you build fences or stables, you may pay some or all of the cost in Stone with each Stone worth 2 Wood." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-54-tax-collector" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "54" :type "Occupation" :name "Tax Collector" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever another player pays building resources to build a Major Improvement, you receive 1 resource of those paid (of your choice). You may pay 1 food to the general supply to receive another of the resources paid." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-55-truffle-digger" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "55" :type "Occupation" :name "Truffle Digger" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use a Family member's Action to take Wood and you have 1/2/3 Wild boar, you receive 1/2/3 additional Food." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-56-understudy" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "56" :type "Occupation" :name "Understudy" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever an Action space is occupied by exactly one of your Family members, you may use that Action space again with a second Family member. (Newborns count as Family members)." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-57-vegetarian" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "57" :type "Occupation" :name "Vegetarian" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "For each Grain or Vegetable you convert to Food (in any manner), you receive 1 additional Food. You may not convert animals to Food for the rest of the game." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-58-village-farmer" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "58" :type "Occupation" :name "Village Farmer" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "If there are still 1/3/6/9 rounds to play, you immediately receive 1/2/3/4 Wood. At the end of the game, all players who have the most plowed fields receive 3 Bonus points each." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-59-wheedler" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "59" :type "Occupation" :name "Wheedler" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you receive Food from an Action space, you receive 1 additional Food. This benefit does not apply to Food gained due to an Improvement or Occupation." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-60-wintercrafter" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "60" :type "Occupation" :name "Wintercrafter" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Between the Field and Feeding phases of each Harvest, you may play a Minor Improvement or pay 2 Food to build a Major Improvement. (Pay costs normally)." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-61-almanac" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "61" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Almanac" :min-players 1 :cost-text "1 Wood,1 Stone" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? true :text "When you play this card, immediately take the Field and Breeding phases of a Harvest on your farmyard." :printed-cost {:wood 1 :stone 1}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-62-animal-farm" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "62" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Animal Farm" :min-players 1 :cost-text "1 Wood" :prerequisites "2 Animal Types" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Once per round, you may return 1 of you animals to the supply for a Guest token, which you place this round as you would a Family member. (The Guest represents the animal.)" :printed-cost {:wood 1}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-63-baking-field" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "63" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Baking Field" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "2 Occupations and 1 Baking Improvement" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "When you Sow, you can plant Grain on this card as you would on a field. When harvesting, you must (and may) immediately Bake this field's harvested Grain. (This card does not count as a field when scoring.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-64-bartering-hut" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "64" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Bartering Hut" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? true :text "When you play this card, immediately buy up to 2 (same or different) animals from the general supply. Pay any 2 building resources for each Sheep, any 3 for each Wild boar, and any 4 for each Cattle." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-65-beehive-oven" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "65" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Beehive Oven" :min-players 1 :cost-text "2 Stone" :prerequisites "" :points-text "1" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use the \"Bake bread\" action, you can use the Beehive Oven to convert up to 1 Grain into 4 Food. Whenever you Bake 1 or more Grain into bread without using the Beehive Oven, you receive 1 additional Food. When you play this card, you can immediately take the \"Bake bread\" action." :printed-cost {:stone 2}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-66-birthstone" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "66" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Birthstone" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you grow your family, you may pay 1 Stone for 1 Bonus point. When you play Birthstone, you may immediately do this for any new Family member that you already received this round." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-67-bountiful-harvest" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "67" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Bountiful Harvest" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "2 Occupations" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "If you harvest at least 2 resources and breed at least 1 animal during a Harvest, place 1 Food from the supply on this card. You may use this Food at any time. At the end of the game, you receive 1 Bonus point for each Food on this card." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-68-chronicle" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "68" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Chronicle" :min-players 1 :cost-text "2 Wood/2 Clay" :prerequisites "1 Occupation" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Place 1 Food on each remaining Major Improvement on the Major Improvements Board. When these Improvements are acquired, you receive the Food." :printed-cost {:wood 2 :clay 2}}
   {:id "original-expansion-g-69-clear-cutting" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "G" :number "69" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Clear Cutting" :min-players 1 :cost-text "1 Wood" :prerequisites "1 Occupation" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you Plow 1 or more fields, you receive 1 Wood from the supply for each field you just plowed." :printed-cost {:wood 1}}
