   {:id "original-expansion-nl-69-mink-breeder" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "69" :type "Occupation" :name "Mink Breeder" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "In each round from Round 5 on, the first player to place their second person on the same gameboard as their first person must first pay you 1 Food." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-70-left-liberal" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "70" :type "Occupation" :name "Left Liberal" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use 1 of the 6 leftmost Action spaces on the first game board, you receive 1 additional Wood." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-71-maidservant" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "71" :type "Occupation" :name "Maidservant" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use the \"Fishing\" Action space or one of its neighbors (\"Day Laborer\", \"Take 1 Reed\", or the Round 4 Action space), you receive 1 additional Food for each person occupying any of these 4 spaces excluding the person you just placed." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-72-salvation-army-officer" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "72" :type "Occupation" :name "Salvation Army Officer" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever, at the start of a round before phase 1, another player has no Food markers, you may give them 1 Food from your personal supply. If you do this, you receive your choice of 1 Grain, 1 Wood, 1 Clay, 1 Reed, or 1 Sheep from the general supply." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-73-companion" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "73" :type "Occupation" :name "Companion" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "In the round you play this card, all Action spaces count as unoccupied for you. (Even if one of your people use it.) From now, Action spaces that are used by another player's last person count as unoccupied for you." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-74-field-messenger" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "74" :type "Occupation" :name "Field Messenger" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Randomly choose 1 of your Unused farmyard spaces. Rules permitting, you may either fence this space or build a stable there without paying Wood. Alternatively, you may Plow 1 field there." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-75-governor-general" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "75" :type "Occupation" :name "Governor General" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "At the end of the game, you receive 1 and a half Bonus points for each room in your Stone house rounded down and your negative points are doubled. (This also applies to Begging cards.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-76-cheese-carrier" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "76" :type "Occupation" :name "Cheese Carrier" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "In the Breeding phase of each Harvest, you receive half a Food from the general supply for each other player who has at least 1 Sheep, rounded up. Also, you receive 1 Food for each other player who has at least 1 Cattle. (Your animals do not count.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-77-kitchen-maid" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "77" :type "Occupation" :name "Kitchen Maid" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Once you have built a Cooking Hearth, alternate placing 1 Food and 1 Grain on each remaining even numbered Round space. Start with 1 Food. At the start of these rounds, you receive the item. (If you already have a Cooking Hearth when you play this card, place the goods immediately.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-78-water-worker" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "78" :type "Occupation" :name "Water Worker" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use the \"Fishing\" Action space or one of its neighbors, \"Day Laborer\", \"Take 1 Reed\", or the Round 4 Action space, you receive 1 additional Reed." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-79-farmer-s-daughter" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "79" :type "Occupation" :name "Farmer's Daughter" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Once you have built a Clay hut, place 1 Grain on each remaining even numbered Round space. At the start of these rounds, you receive the Grain. (If you already have a Clay hut or Stone house when you play this card, place the Grain immediately.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-80-witch-of-haarlem" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "80" :type "Occupation" :name "Witch of Haarlem" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you take Wood/ Clay/ Reed/ Sheep/ Wild Boar/ Food from an Accumulation space, you may convert exactly 1 of them into 1 Clay/ Reed/ Stone/ Wild Boar/ Cattle/ Grain (respectively)." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-81-freedom-fighter" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "81" :type "Occupation" :name "Freedom Fighter" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "When you play this card, pay 2 additional Food. Until the next Harvest, you may use Action spaces even if they are occupied by other players." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-82-knight" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "82" :type "Occupation" :name "Knight" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "In the Field phase of the last Harvest, multiply the number of your Stone rooms by the number of your Cattle. You receive this many Food. If you receive more Food from the Knight alone than is needed to feed your family, take the excess in Bonus pts, 1 to 1 up to 5" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-83-basketmaker-s-son" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "83" :type "Occupation" :name "Basketmaker's Son" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use the Basketmaker's Workshop in a Harvest, you receive 2 additional Grain. For this, you must have at least 3 Family members. (Guests are not counted.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-84-grand-pensionary" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "84" :type "Occupation" :name "Grand Pensionary" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Each round, before the Work phase, you may mark 3 Action spaces. At most 2 of these spaces can be used by others. The third must remain free for you (even if you do not have any people left). You may choose not to use the third space." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-85-gauger" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "85" :type "Occupation" :name "Gauger" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "At any time, any player can use the Gauger to convert 1 Grain into 2 Food. Whenever another player uses the Gauger to convert 1 or more Grain into Food, you receive 1 Food from the general supply." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-86-investor" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "86" :type "Occupation" :name "Investor" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "When you play this card, you may immediately build up to 2 Major Improvements by paying 1 Food each and discarding your entire hand. (You do not need to pay the costs of the Major Improvements)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-87-distant-princess" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "87" :type "Occupation" :name "Distant Princess" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "If there are still 6/9 rounds to play, you immediately receive 3/4 Wood. At the end of the game, the player who grew to 5 Family members last receives 2 Bonus points." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-88-cloth-maker" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "88" :type "Occupation" :name "Cloth Maker" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever another player uses the \"Take 1 Sheep\" Action space, you receive 1 Sheep from the general supply. (If you use the Action space, you do not receive a benefit.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-89-general" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "89" :type "Occupation" :name "General" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "At the end of the game, if you have 2x3 or 3x2 connected Unused farmyard spaces, you receive 9 Bonus points. (Your 6 Unused spaces are still scored as 6 Unused spaces.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-90-woman-weighing-pearls" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "90" :type "Occupation" :name "Woman Weighing Pearls" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever another player uses the \"Fishing\" Action space, you may pay them 1 Food and receive 1 Bonus point." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-91-harlequin" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "91" :type "Occupation" :name "Harlequin" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever the Starting player of the current round uses the \"Traveling Players\" action, you receive 1 Vegetable. Whenever the player in position 2/3/4 uses it, you receive 1 Sheep/ Stone/ Bonus point." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-92-flying-housewife" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "92" :type "Occupation" :name "Flying Housewife" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use your second Family member to use the \"Family growth\" Action space in Stage 2, you may immediately afterward move it and use another Action space. The \"Family growth\" Action space remains occupied by your newborn." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-93-lawyer" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "93" :type "Occupation" :name "Lawyer" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "When you play this card, you receive 2 different building resources of your choice. From Round 13 on, you may use the Round 13 Action space even if it is occupied by another player." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-94-homo-ludens" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "94" :type "Occupation" :name "Homo Ludens" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "In a 4 player game, take the Action cards from the 5 player game and visa versa. At the beginning of each round, choose one randomly. This Action space is available for you only that round. (Fill any Accumulation space once.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-95-navvy" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "95" :type "Occupation" :name "Navvy" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "When you play this card, you may immediately pay 1 Food for 1 Grain. Once each round, whenever you Sow, you may Plow 1 field immediately afterward." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-96-wash-woman" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "96" :type "Occupation" :name "Wash Woman" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use the \"Fishing\" Action space with exactly 3 Food on it, you receive an additional 1 Grain and 1 building resource of your choice." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-97-cheese-seller" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "97" :type "Occupation" :name "Cheese Seller" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "When you play this card, you may immediately buy 1 Sheep and/or 1 Cattle for 1 Food each. Whenever you end a round with the number of your Sheep plus twice the number of your Cattle greater than or equal to the current round number, you receive 1 Food. (If the current round ends with a Harvest, you may count your animals after the Harvest.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-98-ice-skate-sharpener" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "98" :type "Occupation" :name "Ice Skate Sharpener" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "At the end of each Harvest, you may pay 1 Wood and 1 Food to use out of turn an Action space of your choice without placing a person." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-99-prolific-writer" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "99" :type "Occupation" :name "Prolific Writer" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "You receive 2 Food before you pay the costs of playing this Occupation. In the Returning home phase of each Round, you must choose 1 player among those who built or played a new card that round. That player receives 1 Food from the general supply. (You may choose yourself if possible.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-100-glasses-maker" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "100" :type "Occupation" :name "Glasses Maker" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "When you play this card, you receive 1 Reed and 1 Food. Instead of the \"Build Room(s)\" action on the corresponding Action space, you may take the \"Renovate\" action and vice versa. (This card does not effect additional actions on those spaces.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-101-discoverer" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "101" :type "Occupation" :name "Discoverer" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Add 3 to the current round number and place the person who played this Occupation on the corresponding round space. (It is no longer considered part of your family until then.) At the start of that round, you receive the person back, even if you have no room in your home, and you receive 2 Food, 1 Bonus point, and 1 Vegetable." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-102-crown-prince" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "102" :type "Occupation" :name "Crown Prince" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "In Round 14, immediately before the Starting player places his first person, you may use 1 of your people to use all the Action spaces for Rounds 11,12,13 and 14 in any order. Leave your person on the last space you used. The Work phase is over for you. (You cannot place anymore people.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-103-dancer-and-spy" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "103" :type "Occupation" :name "Dancer and Spy" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use the \"Traveling Players\" action on an Action space, you may move any person from an Action space with exactly 1 person on it to \"Traveling players\" also. (They don't use action.) Afterward, you may immediately use the freed Action space with another person." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-104-grain-reaper" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "104" :type "Occupation" :name "Grain Reaper" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use the \"Plow 1 Field\" or \"Plow and/or Sow\" Action space, you may take the Field phase of a Harvest on your farmyard before taking the action. (This does not count as a Harvest.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-105-tree-cutter" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "105" :type "Occupation" :name "Tree Cutter" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "When you play this card, you receive 1 Wood. Whenever you receive 3 or more items of the same type (excluding Wood) from an Accumulation space, you receive 1 Wood. (Accumulation spaces are Action spaces where Goods or Food accumulate.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-106-love-messenger" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "106" :type "Occupation" :name "Love Messenger" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "In the next round and in Round 13 and 14, only you can take a \"Family growth\" Action space with your first person. (Any player can take it with their second person or higher.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-107-matchmaker" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "107" :type "Occupation" :name "Matchmaker" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "When you play this card, you receive 1 Wood, 1 building resource of your choice, 1 Sheep, 1 Wild Boar, 1 Food, 1 Grain and 1 Vegetable. Also, you may receive 2 Bonus points. In the Returning home phase of this round, remove 1 of your Family members from the game completely." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-108-rationalist" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "108" :type "Occupation" :name "Rationalist" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you play an Improvement and you would pay Stone as a building material, you may replace that Stone with the same amount of Clay if you pay an additional 1 Food." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-109-thresher" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "109" :type "Occupation" :name "Thresher" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use the \"Sow and/or Bake bread\", \"Plow 1 Field\", or \"Plow and/or Sow\" Action spaces, you may buy 1 Grain for 1 Food before taking the action." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-110-tree-collector" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "110" :type "Occupation" :name "Tree Collector" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever another player takes 1 to 3 Wood from a Wood Accumulation space with a person, you receive 1 Wood from the general supply. (When you take Wood, you receive no benefit.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-111-assistant-tiller" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "111" :type "Occupation" :name "Assistant Tiller" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use the \"Day Laborer\" Action space, you may also Plow 1 field." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-112-grain-harvester" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "112" :type "Occupation" :name "Grain Harvester" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "When you play this card, you receive 1 Grain. In each Field phase of Harvest, you may harvest 1 additional Grain from each of your Grain fields." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-113-suffragette" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "113" :type "Occupation" :name "Suffragette" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Each Work phase on your first turn, you may pay 2 food to place both your first and second person immediately one after another. If you do this, you must place each person on a different game board. (Then, when it's your second turn, you place your third person.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-114-canal-boatman" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "114" :type "Occupation" :name "Canal Boatman" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use the \"Fishing\" or \"Take 1 Reed\" Action space (on the second game board), you may later in the same round, pay 1 Food to place a person on this card. If you do this, you receive either 3 Stone or 1 Grain and 1 Vegetable." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-115-clay-baker" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "115" :type "Occupation" :name "Clay Baker" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "When you play this card, you receive 2 Clay. At any time you may convert 1 Clay into 1 Food." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-116-potato-eater" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "116" :type "Occupation" :name "Potato Eater" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "In the Feeding phase of each Harvest, your people need only 1 Food each if the Food comes from Vegetables converted in that Feeding phase. (People who are not fed with Vegetables feed normally.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-117-overwinterer" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "117" :type "Occupation" :name "Overwinterer" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "When you play this card, you receive 1 Grain. At the end of each Harvest, you may buy up to 1 Vegetable for 2 Food." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-118-potato-harvester" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "118" :type "Occupation" :name "Potato Harvester" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "When you play this card, you receive 3 Food. For each Vegetable that you receive from your fields in the Field phase of Harvest, you receive 1 additional Food." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-119-collector" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "119" :type "Occupation" :name "Collector" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "This card is an additional Action space for you only. When you use this Action space the 1st/ 2nd/ 3rd/ 4th time, you receive 1 Begging card and 6/7/8/9 different Goods of your choice. (Goods are Grain, Vegetables, building resources and animals.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-nl-120-choir-boy" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "NL" :number "120" :type "Occupation" :name "Choir Boy" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "You may only play this Occupation when you have 3 or less resources and it is Round 11 or before. At the end of the game, you receive 1 Bonus point for each Family member. (Resources are Grain, Vegetables, and building resources. You may return building resources to the general supply for nothing at any time.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-ae8f3419-1-big-backer" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Ö" :number "1" :type "Occupation" :name "Big Backer" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever another player receives 2 or more animals of one type, you can buy one from him. A Sheep costs 2 Food, a Wild boar 3 Food, a Cattle 4 Food." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-ae8f3419-2-action-artist" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Ö" :number "2" :type "Occupation" :name "Action Artist" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use the \"Traveling Players\" action on an Action space, you can return 1 animal of your choice to the general Supply and receive 4 Food in exchange. (You do not need a Cooking Improvement)." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-ae8f3419-3-therapist" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Ö" :number "3" :type "Occupation" :name "Therapist" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "When you play this card, you can pay 2 Food to immediately play 1 further Occupation. Whenever another player plays an Occupation, you can pay him 1 Food. He must then, if possible, play a different Occupation card instead." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-ae8f3419-4-ski-instructor" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Ö" :number "4" :type "Occupation" :name "Ski Instructor" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever another player has Family Growth, he must pay you 1 Food (or beg for the Food, if necessary). You must immediately turn the Ski Instructor face-down when you grow your Family. You no longer receive its benefits, but it still counts as a played Occupation." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-ae8f3419-5-lovable-vagabond" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Ö" :number "5" :type "Occupation" :name "Lovable Vagabond" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you have no more Food during the Feeding phase of a Harvest and should take one of more Begging cards, you receive one fewer Begging card." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-ae8f3419-6-opinion-leader" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Ö" :number "6" :type "Occupation" :name "Opinion Leader" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "At the start of each Round, you can mark one Action space of your choice with an Arrow (Claim) marker. Each player can use this Action space during this Round. (This cannot be used on Action spaces on which Goods are placed). Remove the Arrow marker at the end of each Round." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-ae8f3419-7-building-tycoon" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Ö" :number "7" :type "Occupation" :name "Building Tycoon" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever another player builds at least one Room, you can give him 1 Food and immediately build exactly one Room yourself (You must pay the Building costs for the Room(s))." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-ae8f3419-8-environmentalist" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Ö" :number "8" :type "Occupation" :name "Environmentalist" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you play or buy an Improvement, you can replace 1 Building resource of your choice with 1 Wood." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-ae8f3419-9-family-singers" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Ö" :number "9" :type "Occupation" :name "Family Singers" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "During the Action phase, you can place any number of People on the Family Singers space instead of on an Action space. For each Person you place on the space, you receive 1 Bonus point." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-ae8f3419-10-waltzer" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Ö" :number "10" :type "Occupation" :name "Waltzer" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "You can place 2 People one after another, as long as both Action spaces are on the same board and adjoin one another. (not diagonally)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-ae8f3419-11-magnate" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Ö" :number "11" :type "Occupation" :name "Magnate" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "When you play this card, you immediately receive 2 Stone. At the end of the game, the Player(s) with the most Building resources receive(s) 3 Bonus points." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-ae8f3419-12-child-prodigy" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Ö" :number "12" :type "Occupation" :name "Child Prodigy" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you have Family growth, you can immediately pay 1 (or 2) Wood for 1 (or 2) Bonus points." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-ae8f3419-13-coffee-house" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Ö" :number "13" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Coffee House" :min-players 1 :cost-text "1 Wood,1 Clay,2 Stone" :prerequisites "" :points-text "2" :passing? false :text "The Coffee House is an Action space for all players. Whenever a Player uses the Coffee House, that player and the card's owner each receive 1 Food from the general Supply. (If you use the card yourself, you receive 2 Food.) In the next Round, the Person from this space can be placed before the Starting player places his first Person." :printed-cost {:wood 1 :clay 1 :stone 2}}
   {:id "original-expansion-ae8f3419-14-spielefest" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Ö" :number "14" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Spielefest" :min-players 1 :cost-text "2 Wood,3 Food" :prerequisites "3 Occupations" :points-text "2" :passing? false :text "The Spielefest is an Action space for all players. Whenever a player visits the Spielefest, he pays the owner of this card 1 Food and receives 2 Bonus points. (You can visit the Spielefest yourself.)" :printed-cost {:wood 2 :food 3}}
   {:id "original-expansion-ae8f3419-15-farmers-ball" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Ö" :number "15" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Farmers' Ball" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "3 Occupations" :points-text "1" :passing? false :text "When this card is played, each Player who immediately pays 5 Food into the general Supply receives 3 Bonus points." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-ae8f3419-16-neutrality" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Ö" :number "16" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Neutrality" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "2 Occupations" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "In the next Round, you can only place your People after the other Players have placed all of theirs. For each Person that you place late, you receive 1 Bonus point." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-ae8f3419-17-guest-worker" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Ö" :number "17" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Guest Worker" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "have more Rooms than People" :points-text "1" :passing? false :text "Take a Guest marker. From the next Round, you can place this as you would a Family member. The Guest worker can use the most recent Round card even if it has already been taken. He occupies a Room in your Home and must be fed with 2 Food during the Feeding Phase of each Harvest." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-ae8f3419-18-schnitzel-mallet" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Ö" :number "18" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Schnitzel Mallet" :min-players 1 :cost-text "1 Stone" :prerequisites "2 Occupations" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "For each Cattle that you turn to Food using a Cooking Improvement, you receive 1 additional Food and 1 Bonus point." :printed-cost {:stone 1}}
   {:id "original-expansion-ae8f3419-19-compulsory-education" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Ö" :number "19" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Compulsory Education" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "1 Occupation" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you have Family Growth, you can pay 1 Food to immediately play an Occupation. (If you can also play a Minor Improvement, you must first play the Occupation)." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-ae8f3419-20-emergency-housing" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Ö" :number "20" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Emergency Housing" :min-players 1 :cost-text "1 Wood,1 Reed" :prerequisites "at least 1 built Stable" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Select 1 of your built Stables. It is now a Room for one of your Family members. The Stable loses its original function, but is still worth 1 additional point if fenced." :printed-cost {:wood 1 :reed 1}}
   {:id "original-expansion-ae8f3419-21-vineyard" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Ö" :number "21" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Vineyard" :min-players 1 :cost-text "1 Wood,1 Stone" :prerequisites "" :points-text "1" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use the \"Sow\" action, you can plant up to 3 Food on this card. Up to 3 Food may be planted on it in total. These Food are Sowed in the same way as Grain and are harvested during the Harvest. (This card does not count as a Field when scoring)." :printed-cost {:wood 1 :stone 1}}
   {:id "original-expansion-ae8f3419-22-unusual-architecture" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Ö" :number "22" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Unusual Architecture" :min-players 1 :cost-text "2 Clay" :prerequisites "" :points-text "1" :passing? false :text "Whenever you extend your home with 1 or more Rooms, you receive 2 Food for each new Room." :printed-cost {:clay 2}}
   {:id "original-expansion-ae8f3419-23-lederhosen" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Ö" :number "23" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Lederhosen" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "3 Occupations" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "For each Sheep that you convert to Food, place 1 Food from the general Supply on this card. If, at the end of the game, you have at least as many Food on the Lederhosen as you have Family members, you receive 2 Bonus points; if you have twice as many, you receive 3 Bonus points." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-ae8f3419-24-styrian-oak" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "Ö" :number "24" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Styrian Oak" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "1 Occupation" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Place 5 Food from the general Supply on the Styrian Oak. At the start of each Round, you can return 1 Food to the general Supply. Once during the game, at any time, you can pay the number of Food (0 to 5) remaining on the Styrian Oak to receive 6 Wood from the Supply." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-e76bce6e-1-alchemist" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "ℼ" :number "1" :type "Occupation" :name "Alchemist" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "When you play this card, you receive 2 Wood. Whenever you receive Building resources or animals from an Action space, you may place 1 of the goods received on the space afterward and take 1 Wood or Clay from any Accumulation space." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-e76bce6e-2-altruist" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "ℼ" :number "2" :type "Occupation" :name "Altruist" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Twice during the game, you may use the \"Renovate\" action to convert your Stone house back into a Wooden hut by paying 1 Wood per room and 1 Reed. When you do this, you receive 3 Bonus points per room and you receive 3 Clay." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-e76bce6e-3-backpacker" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "ℼ" :number "3" :type "Occupation" :name "Backpacker" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "In the Returning home phase of each even-numbered round, you may choose to not return home 1 person. When you leave a person on an Action space this way, immediately before the start of the next Work phase, take that action again (and keep space occupied). If you cannot, take 1 Begging card and return him home." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-e76bce6e-4-chisel-maker" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "ℼ" :number "4" :type "Occupation" :name "Chisel Maker" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Place an Arrow marker on a revealed Round Action space and point the Arrow toward nobody. The next player to use this space receives 1 Stone. Whenever any player uses this Action space, point the Arrow toward that player. At the start of each round, the player whom the Arrow points toward receives 1 Wood." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-e76bce6e-5-contortionist" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "ℼ" :number "5" :type "Occupation" :name "Contortionist" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Place 4 Wood, 3 Clay, 2 Reed, and 2 Stone in a container. Whenever you take the \"Traveling Players\" action, draw 2 resources at random. If they are the same, keep both. If they are different keep 1 and return the other to the general supply." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-e76bce6e-6-footman" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "ℼ" :number "6" :type "Occupation" :name "Footman" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Once each round, you may place a person on an Action space without immediately taking the action. Instead, you may take that action immediately after any of your other turns that round. At the end of that round, if you haven't taken the action, you receive 1 Begging card." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-e76bce6e-7-marriage-counselor" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "ℼ" :number "7" :type "Occupation" :name "Marriage Counselor" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever, at the start of a round, another player has at least 2 more Family members than you or all other players have at least 1 more Family member than you, you may pay 1 Food to use 1 Guest token that round." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-e76bce6e-8-master-carpenter" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "ℼ" :number "8" :type "Occupation" :name "Master Carpenter." :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "You can build fences around your rooms by fencing all 4 sides of a room. You may not fence more than 1 room each round. Each fenced room can hold an additional Family member. Fenced rooms are not pastures." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-e76bce6e-9-pest-exterminator" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "ℼ" :number "9" :type "Occupation" :name "Pest Exterminator" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "If you have no built fences, place 1 of your fences on each of the 14 round cards, both revealed and unrevealed. Whenever you use an Action space with your fence on it, you may return the fence to your supply. At the end of the game, you receive 1 Bonus point for each fence returned after the first 6." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-e76bce6e-10-professor" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "ℼ" :number "10" :type "Occupation" :name "Professor" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "After you play this card, discard all the remaining Occupations in your hand and draw 7 new Occupations. You can play an additional Occupation immediately for 2 Food. (You must pay any additional costs of the new Occupation)." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-e76bce6e-11-sunrise-herder" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "ℼ" :number "11" :type "Occupation" :name "Sunrise Herder" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Once each round, you may skip placing your first Family member and receive 1 animal. You must pay 1 Food if you receive a Cattle. (You place the person later. You may only do this if every player has at least 1 person still to place.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-e76bce6e-12-wounded-veteran" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "ℼ" :number "12" :type "Occupation" :name "Wounded Veteran" :min-players 4 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "At the start of each round, you receive 2 Food from the general supply. Whenever you take Building resources or animals from an Accumulation space, you must leave 1 of them on the space." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-e76bce6e-13-angry-duck" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "ℼ" :number "13" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Angry Duck" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "When you play this card, if there is any Food on future Round spaces that you would later receive, you may place some or all of that Food on this card. At the end of the game, you receive 1/2/3/4/5 Bonus points for 1/2/3/5/8 Food on this card. (You may not use the Food on this card.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-e76bce6e-14-fertility-shrine" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "ℼ" :number "14" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Fertility Shrine" :min-players 1 :cost-text "2 Stone" :prerequisites "" :points-text "-1" :passing? false :text "In the Breeding phase of each Harvest, if 2 or more animal types in your farm breed, you may return 2 newborn animals to the general supply and immediately take a \"Family growth even without room\" action. (You must have room for the baby animals on your farm first.)" :printed-cost {:stone 2}}
   {:id "original-expansion-e76bce6e-15-fishing-pier" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "ℼ" :number "15" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Fishing Pier" :min-players 1 :cost-text "2 Wood" :prerequisites "1 Occupation" :points-text "1" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use the \"Fishing\" Action space, you may also take 1 Building resource from any other Action space." :printed-cost {:wood 2}}
   {:id "original-expansion-e76bce6e-16-gardeners-bothy" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "ℼ" :number "16" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Gardeners' Bothy" :min-players 1 :cost-text "2 Wood,1 Reed" :prerequisites "" :points-text "1" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use the \"Plow 1 Field\" Action space, you may immediately afterward move that person to this card to receive 1 Grain. Whenever you use the \"Plow 1 field and/or Sow\" Action space, you may immediately afterward move that person to this card to receive 1 Vegetable." :printed-cost {:wood 2 :reed 1}}
   {:id "original-expansion-e76bce6e-17-geode" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "ℼ" :number "17" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Geode" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "Have 1 Stone" :points-text "" :passing? true :text "Draw 3 Minor Improvements randomly from the deck. You may immediately play 1 of these Minor Improvements (pay costs and fulfill prerequisites normally), or add it to your hand. Discard the other 2 Improvements." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-e76bce6e-18-landscape-design" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "ℼ" :number "18" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Landscape Design" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Your fields no longer need to be orthogonally adjacent to each other. Fields plowed at the same time must be adjacent. At the end of the game, you receive 1/2/3 Bonus points for 3/4/5 fields that are not orthogonally adjacent to another field." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-e76bce6e-19-market-square" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "ℼ" :number "19" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Market Square" :min-players 1 :cost-text "2 Wood" :prerequisites "" :points-text "1" :passing? false :text "When you play this card, place 4 Building resources of your choice from the general supply on it. Whenever any player (including you) receives Building resources from an Action space, they may exchange one for a different resource on this card. Any player who does this must pay you 1 Food." :printed-cost {:wood 2}}
   {:id "original-expansion-e76bce6e-20-meeting-post" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "ℼ" :number "20" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Meeting Post" :min-players 1 :cost-text "1 Wood/1 Clay" :prerequisites "" :points-text "1" :passing? false :text "When you play this card, every player must place 1 Occupation from their hand face up on the board. Add random Occupations from the deck until there are 5. Whenever any player plays an Occupation, that player may play 1 of these Occupations instead of 1 from their hand. If so, you get any Food paid." :printed-cost {:wood 1 :clay 1}}
   {:id "original-expansion-e76bce6e-21-pitchfork" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "ℼ" :number "21" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Pitchfork" :min-players 1 :cost-text "1 Wood,1 Stone" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you extend or renovate your home, you may pay with Reed directly from Accumulation spaces." :printed-cost {:wood 1 :stone 1}}
   {:id "original-expansion-e76bce6e-22-retirement" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "ℼ" :number "22" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Retirement" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "1 Occupation" :points-text "1" :passing? false :text "Immediately turn all of your Occupations before you face down. At the start of each round, you receive 1 Food as long as you have no face up Occupations. All effects of the face down cards are forfeited but they still count as played Occupations." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-e76bce6e-23-shelter-in-the-field" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "ℼ" :number "23" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Shelter in the Field" :min-players 1 :cost-text "3 Wood/3 Clay,1 Reed" :prerequisites "1 planted field" :points-text "1" :passing? false :text "This card can hold 1 Family member who can only use the \"Take 1 Grain\", \"Take 1 Vegetable\", \"Plow 1 field\" or \"Sow and/or Bake\" Action spaces. This Family member cannot be moved to your home." :printed-cost {:wood 3 :clay 3 :reed 1}}
   {:id "original-expansion-e76bce6e-24-spars" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "ℼ" :number "24" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Spars" :min-players 1 :cost-text "1 Wood" :prerequisites "See Below" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you build a Room or Renovate your home, you may receive 1 Negative point instead of paying the required 1 or 2 Reed. In a 2 or 3 player game, you may only play this Minor Improvement on the \"1 Major or Minor Improvement\" Action space." :printed-cost {:wood 1}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wa-1-clutch-drive" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WA" :number "1" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Clutch Drive" :min-players 1 :cost-text "1 Clay" :prerequisites "1 Occupation" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use the Round space with the number that is equal to the total of Wood in your supply, you receive 1 Wood from the general supply afterwards." :printed-cost {:clay 1}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wa-2-ardennes" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WA" :number "2" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Ardennes" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "6 Clay" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Place 1 Wood on each remaining even-numbered Round space. At the start of these Rounds, you receive the Wood." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wa-3-beer-museum" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WA" :number "3" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Beer Museum" :min-players 1 :cost-text "2 Clay,2 Wood" :prerequisites "2 Grain" :points-text "2" :passing? false :text "In the Feeding phase of each harvest, you may convert 1 Grain to 6 Food, but you only receive the Food in the Field phase of the next harvest. (You do not need any improvement with the bread symbol for this conversion.)" :printed-cost {:clay 2 :wood 2}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wa-4-begging-letter" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WA" :number "4" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Begging Letter" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "No Food" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Each of your opponents must give you 1 Minor Improvement card from their hand. Choose 1 of those cards and take it into your hand. Then shuffle the remaining cards and the Begging Letter and deal 1 card at random to each of your opponents. Immediately afterwards, you receive an additional \"Minor Improvement\" action." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wa-5-beer-parlor" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WA" :number "5" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Beer Parlor" :min-players 1 :cost-text "2 Clay" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "When you play this card, you receive 1 Grain. Before each Returning home phase, if all of your Family members were placed on the same game board, you may convert 1 Grain from your supply into 3 Food. (All the Action spaces are distributed on 3 game boards. You do not need any improvement with the bread symbol for this conversion.)" :printed-cost {:clay 2}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wa-6-beer-table" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WA" :number "6" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Beer Table" :min-players 1 :cost-text "2 Wood" :prerequisites "No Grain" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "At the end of the Field phase of each harvest, you may pay 1 Grain for 2 Bonus points. If you do, all other players receive 1 Food from the general supply." :printed-cost {:wood 2}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wa-7-comic-shop" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WA" :number "7" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Comic Shop" :min-players 1 :cost-text "1 Wood,1 Clay" :prerequisites "play in Round 8 or 9" :points-text "3" :passing? false :text "This card is an additional Action space for all players. It can only be used if the player using it has no more Family members in his home afterwards. In the Work phase of the following 2 rounds, that player may place up to 2 persons whenever it is his turn." :printed-cost {:wood 1 :clay 1}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wa-8-steam-engine" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WA" :number "8" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Steam Engine" :min-players 1 :cost-text "2 Wood" :prerequisites "" :points-text "1" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use an accumulation space with the last person you place each Work phase, you can also take a \"Bake bread\" Action afterwards. (Accumulation spaces are those Action spaces on which goods or Food accumulate.)" :printed-cost {:wood 2}}
