   {:id "original-expansion-wm-3-apple-picker" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "3" :type "Occupation" :name "Apple Picker" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use the \"Take 1 Grain\" or \"Take 1 Vegetable\" action, you receive an additional 1 Wood and 1 Food." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-4-bargaining-baker" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "4" :type "Occupation" :name "Bargaining Baker" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you build a Baking Improvement with the bread symbol, you receive 1 Grain before building the Improvement. Whenever you build an Oven, pay 1 Building resource less of your choice. (An Oven is a Baking Improvement with \"Oven\" in the name.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-5-bee-keeper" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "5" :type "Occupation" :name "Bee Keeper" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "When you play this card, immediately build 1 stable without paying Wood and place it on its side. This stable loses its regular animal functions. (It is still worth 1 additional point if fenced.) In the Feeding phase of each Harvest, you receive 1 Food as long as the stable is on your farm." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-6-borrower" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "6" :type "Occupation" :name "Borrower" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "When you play this card, you receive 7 Food and 2 Begging cards. At any time, you may pay 3 Food to discard one of these 2 Begging cards or a Begging card you received instead of paying 1 Food to feed your family." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-7-branch-collector" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "7" :type "Occupation" :name "Branch Collector" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use Clay or Stone for an extension, Renovation, or Improvement, you receive 1 Wood from the general supply (for each new Room, Renovation, or Improvement) before paying its costs." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-8-bread-carrier" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "8" :type "Occupation" :name "Bread Carrier" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Once any player has built an Oven, place 1 Food on the remaining Round spaces. At the start of these rounds, you receive the Food. (If an Oven has already been built, place the Food immediately. If multiple Ovens are built, you only receive the Food once.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-9-chemist" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "9" :type "Occupation" :name "Chemist" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use a person's action to take Wood from a building resource Accumulation space, you may immediately place 1 Clay from your supply on another building resource Accumulation space to receive 2 Food." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-10-cloister-dweller" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "10" :type "Occupation" :name "Cloister Dweller" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "At the end of the game, you receive 1 Bonus point for each of the 5 columns of your farmyard that is either all rooms, all fields or all in the same pasture." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-11-contractor" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "11" :type "Occupation" :name "Contractor" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you build a room, renovate your home, or build a Major Improvement, you can replace up to 1 Building resource of your choice with 1 Food." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-12-covetous-farmer" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "12" :type "Occupation" :name "Covetous Farmer" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Once each round, during one of your turns, you may take 1 Building resource from the general supply of a type that you do not have and every other player does have." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-13-cowboy" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "13" :type "Occupation" :name "Cowboy" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "You can use the \"Take 1 Sheep\", \"Wild boar\" or \"Cattle\" Action spaces even if they are occupied. If you do this, take 1 animal of that type. Additionally, you can keep 2 animals of the same type on 1 of your Unused farmyard spaces. (The space still counts as unused.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-14-crop-rotator" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "14" :type "Occupation" :name "Crop Rotator" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you remove the last Grain/Vegetable from a field, you may immediately Sow a Vegetable/ Grain in that field. When you play this card, immediately take 1 Grain or Vegetable from each of your fields and place them in your supply." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-15-debris-dealer" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "15" :type "Occupation" :name "Debris Dealer" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "When you renovate your Clay hut, you receive 2 Clay afterward. Once you live in a Clay hut or Stone house, whenever another player renovates their Wooden/Clay hut, you receive 2 Wood/Clay." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-16-diplomat" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "16" :type "Occupation" :name "Diplomat" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Once during Round 14, you may use an Action space even if it is occupied by other players. If you play this card in Round 7 or before, you may do this twice instead." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-17-engineer" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "17" :type "Occupation" :name "Engineer" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you play an Improvement, you receive 1 Food before paying the costs of the Improvement. If the Improvement has a printed Stone cost, you receive 2 Food instead of 1." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-18-expert-builder" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "18" :type "Occupation" :name "Expert Builder" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever any player (including you) builds 1 or more rooms, they must place 1 resource of those paid on this card. You may use these resources to pay for your extensions or renovations." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-19-family-planner" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "19" :type "Occupation" :name "Family Planner" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Add 4, 7 and 10 to the current round and place up to 1 person still in your supply on each corresponding Round space. At the start of these rounds and not earlier, you may take the person as a new Family member, if you have room. It counts as a Newborn, and may take actions the following round." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-20-farm-school-graduate" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "20" :type "Occupation" :name "Farm School Graduate" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "You may only play this card as your first Occupation. From now, you may not use any Occupation action on any Action space. At the start of each Harvest, you may pay 2 Food to play an Occupation." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-21-fence-dealer" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "21" :type "Occupation" :name "Fence Dealer" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "You may only build 12 fences. (Remove the other 3 fences from the game.) Whenever you build fences you may build 2 fences for every 1 Wood paid." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-22-food-connoisseur" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "22" :type "Occupation" :name "Food Connoisseur" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Pile (from bottom to top) 1 Clay, Vegetable, Stone, Grain, Wood, Reed on this card. Whenever you use a person to take Food from the \"Day Laborer\", \"Fishing\" or \"Traveling Players\" Action space, additionally take the top item on this card." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-23-forest-farmer" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "23" :type "Occupation" :name "Forest Farmer" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Place 3 Arrow markers on this card. Each round, between the Work and Returning home phase, you may pay 1 Wood and return 1 marker to move one of your people from the \"Plow 1 field\" or \"Plow 1 field and/or Sow\" Action space to a free Action space and take the action." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-24-gem-hunter" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "24" :type "Occupation" :name "Gem Hunter" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use a person to take Clay from a Building resource Accumulation space, you may also receive 1 Stone. In Round 9 or before, if there are 3 or more Clay on the space, you must leave 1 Clay on the space to receive the Stone." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-25-godfather" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "25" :type "Occupation" :name "Godfather" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use an Action space orthogonally adjacent to an occupied \"Family growth\" Action space from stage 2 or stage 5, you receive 1 Grain immediately before." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-26-hedge-master" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "26" :type "Occupation" :name "Hedge Master" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you build fences, you receive 1 Bonus point. When you play this card, you may immediately build fences." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-27-heiress" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "27" :type "Occupation" :name "Heiress" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "At the start of round 6/10/13, you may (before phase 1) build 1 Wooden/ Clay/ Stone room if your home is made of the same material. Pay 1 less Clay for the Clay room and 2 less Stone for the Stone room. (When you play this card, place the Room tiles on the corresponding round spaces.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-28-herdsman" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "28" :type "Occupation" :name "Herdsman" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use the \"Day Laborer\" Action space, you receive 1 additional Sheep. From round 6, you can choose to receive 1 Wild boar instead." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-29-hill-farmer" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "29" :type "Occupation" :name "Hill Farmer" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you build 1 or more fences or Plow 1 or more fields, you receive 2/1 Food if you have exactly 2/3 rooms." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-30-hoarder" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "30" :type "Occupation" :name "Hoarder" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Each Harvest, you can place 1 Building resource on this card from your supply. At the end of the game, you receive 1/2/3/5 Bonus Points for 1/2/3/4 different resources on this card." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-31-humble-farmboy" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "31" :type "Occupation" :name "Humble Farmboy" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "If there are still 1/3/6/9 rounds to play, you immediately receive 1/2/3/4 Wood. At the end of the game, all players with the fewest cards in front of them receive 3 Bonus Points. (Count Occupations plus Improvements and exclude Begging cards.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-32-hunter" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "32" :type "Occupation" :name "Hunter" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you receive animals outside the Breeding phase of a Harvest, you may immediately convert them into Food. Take 2/3/4 Food for each Sheep/Wild boar/Cattle converted." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-33-lady-in-waiting" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "33" :type "Occupation" :name "Lady in Waiting" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "If you play this card during Stage 1, place 1 person still in your supply on Round 12. At the start of this round, you can pay 2 Food to move this person into your home whether or not you have room. It counts as an adult Family member and may take actions starting Round 12." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-34-livestock-keeper" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "34" :type "Occupation" :name "Livestock Keeper" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "When you play this card, you receive 1 Wild boar. If you already have a Wild boar, you receive 1 Cattle instead. In the Breeding phase of each Harvest, you may pay 1 Food to receive 2 offspring of exactly 1 animal type that breeds instead of 1." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-35-mailman" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "35" :type "Occupation" :name "Mailman" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Place 2 Wood, 2 Clay, 1 Reed, and 1 Stone on four different revealed Action spaces respectively (occupied or unoccupied). Afterward, any player (including you) who uses one of these spaces may also take the extra resource(s) by paying you 1 Food first." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-36-master-cook" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "36" :type "Occupation" :name "Master Cook" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Each round, instead of placing your first Family member on an Action space, you may place it on this card and receive 2 Food and 1 Guest token to place that round. (You may not do this if you will be placing more people after your first without another player placing in between.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-37-master-stableman" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "37" :type "Occupation" :name "Master Stableman" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use a person's action to take 2 or more animals from an Accumulation space, you can also build up to 2 stables, at a cost of 1 Wood each, before taking the animals." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-38-minimalist" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "38" :type "Occupation" :name "Minimalist" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "At the end of the game, you receive 9/6/4/2 Bonus points for having 0/1/2/3 Improvements in front of you." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-39-pawnbroker" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "39" :type "Occupation" :name "Pawnbroker" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "At any time, you may convert all the printed Victory points (if any) of an Improvement in front of you to 3 Food per point. After, you may not return or remove the Improvement and you no longer receive its Victory points. If Pawnbroker gets turned face down or discarded, you still lose the points." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-40-permaculturist" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "40" :type "Occupation" :name "Permaculturist" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "You may sow Grain on Unused farmyard spaces. Planted spaces count as Grain fields and do not need to be adjacent to your existing plowed fields. You may move Grain from these fields to the general supply at any time and you must before scoring (or if this card gets removed or turned face down)." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-41-politician" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "41" :type "Occupation" :name "Politician" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Twice each round, you may exchange 1 Reed for 1 Stone, or 1 Stone for 1 Reed. When you play this card, you receive 1 Stone." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-42-remodeler" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "42" :type "Occupation" :name "Remodeler" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "When you renovate your Wooden hut, you may first return 1 built stable to extend your hut by 1 Wooden room for free before paying the costs of the Renovation. (The stable can be rebuilt later)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-43-resource-lender" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "43" :type "Occupation" :name "Resource Lender" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you receive Building resources from an Action space, instead of placing them in your supply, you may add 1 resource of 1 type received and place them all on the next Round spaces with 1 per space (in any order and discard any excess). At the start of these rounds, you receive the resource." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-44-silo-girl" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "44" :type "Occupation" :name "Silo Girl" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Once you live in a Stone house, place 1 Grain on each remaining even Round space and 1 Vegetable on each remaining odd Round space. At the start of these rounds, you receive the resources. (If you already live in a Stone house, place the resources immediately.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-45-stable-deliveryman" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "45" :type "Occupation" :name "Stable Deliveryman" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Add 3, 5, 7 and 9 to the current round and place up to 1 of your stables on each remaining corresponding Round space. At the start of these rounds you may pay 1 Wood to build that stable immediately. (If you don't, return that stable to your supply. Until then you cannot build that stable.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-46-stone-curator" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "46" :type "Occupation" :name "Stone Curator" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use a Stone Accumulation space, you receive 1 additional Food. At the end of the game, you receive 1 Bonus point for every 2 rooms in your Stone house and every 2 Improvements with a printed Stone cost." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-47-storehouse-minder" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "47" :type "Occupation" :name "Storehouse Minder" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "When you play this card, you may place 1 to 4 building resources of different types on it from your supply. At the start of each Harvest, choose up to 2 resource types currently on this card and add 1 of each from the general supply. Each round, you may take all the resources of any 1 type remaining." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-48-sunday-worker" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "48" :type "Occupation" :name "Sunday Worker" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Once during Rounds 7 and 14, you may pay 1 Food to take one of your peoples' actions twice. If you use an Accumulation space with that action, you get double the amount of Goods and/or Food." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-49-sunrise-admirer" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "49" :type "Occupation" :name "Sunrise Admirer" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "At the start of each of the next 3 rounds, you may pay 2 Food to Plow 1 of the three Eastern-most spaces on your farmyard (the farm side opposite your home) if they are unused. (Normal plowing rules still apply.) If you choose not to, discard the Sunrise Admirer." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-50-tapestry-weaver" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "50" :type "Occupation" :name "Tapestry Weaver" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you have at least 3 Sheep during the Field phase of a Harvest, place 1 Food from the general supply in your home. You may only place 1 Food per room. You cannot use these Food, but each is worth 1 Bonus point at the end of the game." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-51-tavern-keeper" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "51" :type "Occupation" :name "Tavern Keeper" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "At the start of each Harvest you receive 1 Food and 1 Grain if you have at least 1 room in your home that is not occupied by a Family member. At the end of the game, you receive 1 Bonus Point for every empty room." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-52-tile-maker" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "52" :type "Occupation" :name "Tile Maker" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "If there are 1/3/6/9 rounds to play you receive 1/2/3/4 Clay. At the end of the game all players with a Clay hut receive 2 Bonus points. (This card does not give Bonus points for a Stone house.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-53-village-fool" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "53" :type "Occupation" :name "Village Fool" :min-players 1 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "At the start of each round, you may place 1 card face down from your hand under Village Fool. That card can no longer be used for the rest of the game. At the end of the game, you receive 1 Bonus point for each card under Village Fool except the 3rd, 5th, 7th and 9th." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-54-wheelbarrow-pusher" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "54" :type "Occupation" :name "Wheelbarrow Pusher" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use a person's action to take exactly 1 resource from a Building resource Accumulation space, you receive an additional 1 Building resource of your choice or 1 Food. In a 4 or 5 player game, you instead receive an additional 1 Building resource of your choice and 1 Food." :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-55-wood-worker" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "55" :type "Occupation" :name "Wood Worker" :min-players 3 :cost-text "" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "Whenever you use any Action space, immediately afterward you may place 1 Food from your supply on the space to receive 1 Wood. (The next player to use this Action space receives the Food.)" :printed-cost {}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-56-almshouse" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "56" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Almshouse" :min-players 1 :cost-text "1 Wood,1 Reed" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? false :text "At the end of the Feeding phase of each Harvest, you may discard 1 Begging card that you received in any Harvest because you paid 1 Food less to feed your family." :printed-cost {:wood 1 :reed 1}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-57-animal-nursery" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "57" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Animal Nursery" :min-players 1 :cost-text "2 Wood" :prerequisites "" :points-text "1" :passing? false :text "You may place newborn animals of any type on this card immediately after their birth. They cannot be used for any purpose or moved off this card, but are counted at the end of the game. (This card does not count as a pasture or stable.)" :printed-cost {:wood 2}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-58-apple-tree" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "58" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Apple Tree" :min-players 1 :cost-text "1 Wood" :prerequisites "1 empty field" :points-text "1" :passing? false :text "Place 1 Wood from the general supply on an empty field. This field still counts as a field, but can no longer be used for Sowing or other uses. In the Field phase of each Harvest, you receive 1 Food." :printed-cost {:wood 1}}
   {:id "original-expansion-wm-59-apprenticeship" :edition "Original" :pack "Expansion" :deck "WM" :number "59" :type "Minor Improvement" :name "Apprenticeship" :min-players 1 :cost-text "1 Food" :prerequisites "" :points-text "" :passing? true :text "Immediately play an Occupation if you have fewer Occupations than each other player." :printed-cost {:food 1}}
